<article class="env-definition" id="02Q1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02Q1">Definition <span data-tag="02Q1">42.68.31</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian local domain of dimension $1$ with residue field $\kappa $. Let $K$ be the fraction field of $A$. We define the <em>tame symbol</em> of $A$ to be the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  K^* \times K^* \longrightarrow \kappa ^*, \quad (x, y) \longmapsto d_ A(x, y)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $d_ A(x, y)$ is extended to $K^* \times K^*$ by the multiplicativity of Lemma <a href="/tag/02Q0" data-tag="02Q0">42.68.30</a>. </p>
</article>